# Local secrets only. The SDK's default template ignores the generated
# bindings (dagger.gen.go, internal/dagger), assuming the engine regenerates
# them on demand; ci-debs commits them instead (design: "generated bindings
# (committed, like internal/bpf)") so a fresh checkout vets and builds the
# module without an engine, exactly like the committed bpf2go bindings let
# `go build` work without clang. `dagger develop` rewrites both files; those
# diffs are reviewable like any generated artifact.
/.env
/internal/telemetry
